      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/nikowl/status/2007321773961097574",
      "text": "Much has been said about the lower box-office performance of the ongoing Metro Manila Film Festival. #MMFF51 #MMFF2025 \n\nAt this point, any claims about box office performance are merely hearsay, as the MMFF and the producers/exhibitors have agreed not to disclose box office numbers until the festival concludes, demonstrating solidarity for all entries. \n\nQuality can't also be called out, as at least five of this year's entries have all enjoyed a decent/great amount of appreciation from critics and audiences alike-- Bar Boys: After School, Call Me Mother, I'mPerfect, Manila's Finest, and Unmarry.\n\nBut as they say, when there's smoke, there's fire.\n\nI do think it's obvious what the two factors are that changed within the last two years since they last hit the billion-peso mark. \n\n(1/4)",
      "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
